{"allowed_english": ["fppf", "A", "B"], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "generation_contexts": [{"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:algebraic:inventory:algebraic:04X1:paragraph/0003", "hash": "sha256:244423dae098f675e0ae6fa378e21759764029a08c3636917f97effc412bc279", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 92898, "byte_start": 92609, "file": "algebraic.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:ad691d606f2958f728e6f863c8a5b23404defdb3697e7985f561e4e87d5d127d", "line_end": 2526, "line_start": 2522}, "owner_tag": "04X1", "parent_tag": "04X1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04X1", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:69c656d091ca99b60dd0b0ff73cdb3b4ce315a4610b7de5c6061a6689a83454e", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is not true (in general) that the restriction of an algebraic space\nover the bigger site is an algebraic space over the smaller site (simply\nby reasons of cardinality). Hence we can only ever use a simple lemma of this\nkind to enlarge the base category and never to shrink it.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2d02d4817dca0e49763b7503788042c67875046d1732aa7b779382a71438060f", "unit_id": "inventory:algebraic:04X1:paragraph/0003"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:algebraic:inventory:algebraic:04X3:proof/0001", "hash": "sha256:459ef00719192de9b8ab5d5ffd6af005d1fecfcc665cc6369588de165f499dba", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 94360, "byte_start": 94075, "file": "algebraic.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:a02c8b914c4fa202f062f3557172047ed3431545761fc604d0d8602dd455e0d7", "line_end": 2564, "line_start": 2558}, "owner_tag": "04X3", "parent_tag": "04X1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04X1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f^{-1}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-bigger-site}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-change-big-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:924c753dc04eebc89d08a1c4ba0f7f0ffdff54529e518a2aeeae109ec1f257ff", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:868bbe74cf81d8d114d6129d9315209cdd19dbd8beeb5aae478850c8663bb3a4", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThe statement on morphism categories is a consequence of the more general\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe characterization of the ``essential image'' follows from the description\nof <MATH_0001> in the proof of\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0e673986c806ca599a3840c332144dfd73f21120fc1278b8ddb91bfbf1edb5c1", "unit_id": "inventory:algebraic:04X3:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:algebraic:inventory:algebraic:04X4:paragraph/0001", "hash": "sha256:022b39b42f678ada7e23dea6a03a3ef5d96a6ff9b5b320cead7e05a9a5a286e4", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 94657, "byte_start": 94431, "file": "algebraic.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:3daab0f49533176008f74270efc4778432173a2d3e1139e8dac14bc2696509bb", "line_end": 2573, "line_start": 2570}, "owner_tag": "04X4", "parent_tag": "04X4", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04X4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S \\to S'$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:08eae98cf3075e3092ed363c012572b38e9b36b5cd43bd5f05aa0e522e8e5bd2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a1a87a00094806379fb9dd7d9c9cde8307bfc710b0dce755b5f51c7ba7ce27bf", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we briefly discuss what happens when we change base schemes.\nThe upshot is that given a morphism <MATH_0001> of base schemes, any algebraic\nstack over <MATH_0002> can be viewed as an algebraic stack over <MATH_0003>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dc200f20e43f0f1323ed001b3902d420efb23fcc66d8e2251d31242ed699de6d", "unit_id": "inventory:algebraic:04X4:paragraph/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:algebraic:inventory:algebraic:04X5:proof/0001", "hash": "sha256:2e70cb9ae45988b109d4db521ff8d08bd130f0ae4e211a542c8e0e93a246918e", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 96038, "byte_start": 95345, "file": "algebraic.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:bc6e5b6138700709689b6d5f7a42ca7993cf4e32d64fcfcea747b578e5641ecb", "line_end": 2614, "line_start": 2600}, "owner_tag": "04X5", "parent_tag": "04X4", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04X4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j : (\\Sch/S)_{fppf} \\to (\\Sch/S')_{fppf}$", "MATH_0002": "$S/S'$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S')_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X} = [U/R]$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{X}' = \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X}' = [U'/R']$", "MATH_0008": "$p$", "MATH_0009": "$U' \\to S$", "MATH_0010": "$R' \\to S$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{X} = [U'/R']$", "MATH_0012": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-localize-stacks}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a044